window.docContents[72].resolve({"/Appendix/#section-chapter-4-decidability-finiteness-and-degrees-results":{"contents":"* good_card_edgeFinset: the number of edges of G depends only on\n[Fintype G.edgeSet]; contrast bad_card_edgeFinset, which needlessly assumes\n[Fintype V] and [DecidableRel G.Adj].* degree_completeBipartiteGraph_inl / degree_completeBipartiteGraph_inr:\nvertices in the two parts of K[s, t] have degree t and s.* degree_pathNat: degrees in the infinite path graph on ℕ, which is locally\nfinite without having a finite vertex type.* degree_blowUpN / IsRegularOfDegree.blowUpN: each vertex of the n-uniform\nblow-up G[n] has degree n times its degree in G, so the blow-up of a\nd-regular graph is d * n-regular.* isRegularOfDegree_card_sub_one_iff_eq_top: a graph on a finite vertex type is\nregular of degree |V| - 1 iff it is complete.* sum_degrees_eq_twice_card_edges': the handshake lemma with minimal instance\narguments, dropping the [DecidableRel G.Adj] of the Mathlib version; the\nFintype diamond this exposes is closed by Subsingleton.elim.* IsRegularOfDegree.two_mul_card_edgeFinset / IsRegularOfDegree.card_edgeFinset:\na d-regular graph on n vertices has d * n / 2 edges.* card_hypercubeVert: the hypercube Q[n] has 2 ^ n vertices.* IsRegularOfDegree.hypercube: the hypercube Q[n] is n-regular.* card_edgeFinset_hypercube: the hypercube Q[n] has n * 2 ^ (n - 1) edges.* degree_mycielskian_left: the degree of a left vertex v ₗ of the Mycielskian is\ntwice the degree of v.* Graphic.exists_card_eq: a graphic multiset m is the degree multiset of a graph\nwith exactly m.card vertices.* graphic_degreeMultiset / graphic_degreeSequence: the degree multiset, and\ndegree sequence, of a finite simple graph are graphic.* degree_coneGraph_none: the new vertex of coneGraph H s has degree s.card, a\nkey ingredient of the Havel–Hakimi theorem.* erdos_gallai / havel_hakimi: the two characterizations of graphic multisets.\nBoth are stated but not proved (each is a sorry); havel_hakimi is used only\nto give a DecidablePred Graphic instance that #eval! can run.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* degree_mycielskian_right / degree_mycielskian_none: a right vertex v ᵣ of the\nMycielskian has degree one more than v, and the apex has degree |V|.* card_edgeFinset_mycielskian: the Mycielskian mμ[G] has 3 * |E| + |V|\nedges.* maxDegree_mycielskian / minDegree_mycielskian: the maximum and minimum degrees\nof mμ[G] are max (2 * Δ(G)) (Fintype.card V) and min (2 * δ(G)) (δ(G) + 1).* Graphic.even_sum: a graphic multiset has an even sum.* degree_coneGraph_some / degreeMultiset_coneGraph: the remaining degrees of\nconeGraph H s, and its degree multiset.\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Results","header":"Chapter 4: Decidability, Finiteness and Degrees (Results)","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-4-decidability-finiteness-and-degrees-results"},"/Appendix/#section-notation":{"contents":"This guide introduces quite a bit of \"standard\" graph theory notation not found in\nMathlib.\n\n* Notation* Description* Definition / Target\n* K[n]* Complete graph on n vertices* completeGraph (Fin n)\n* E[n]* Empty graph on n vertices* emptyGraph (Fin n)\n* C[n]* Cycle graph on n vertices* cycleGraph n\n* K[s, t]* Complete bipartite graph* completeBipartiteGraph (Fin s) (Fin t)\n* L[G]* Line graph of a graph G* lineGraph G\n* P[n]* Path graph on n vertices* pathGraph n\n* Q[n]* n-dimensional hypercube* hypercube n\n* v[a, b, …]* Hypercube vertex (open HypercubeVert)* ((((), a), b), …)\n* G[n]* n-uniform blow-up of a graph G* blowUpN G n\n* mμ[G]* Mycielskian of a graph G* mycielskian G\n* v ₗ* \"Left\" copy of v in the Mycielskian* mycielskian.left v\n* v ᵣ* \"Right\" copy of v in the Mycielskian* mycielskian.right v\n* mμᵥ^n V* Vertices of the n-th iterated Mycielskian* MycielskianVert V n\n* mμ^n G* n-th iterated Mycielskian of a graph G* iterMycielskian G n\n* Kn[n, k]* Kneser graph on k-subsets of Fin n* kneserGraph (Fin n) k\n* T[n, r]* Turán graph on n vertices with r parts* turanGraph n r\n* Σg H* Disjoint union of a family of graphs H i* SimpleGraph.sigma H\n* x ⊕ₕ y* Componentwise xor of hypercube vertices* HypercubeVert.xor x y\n* G ⊗g H* Tensor product of G and H* SimpleGraph.tensorProd G H\n* ⨂g i, G i* Tensor product of a family of graphs* SimpleGraph.piTensorProd G\n* δ(G)* Minimum degree of a graph G* SimpleGraph.minDegree G\n* Δ(G)* Maximum degree of a graph G* SimpleGraph.maxDegree G\n* τ G* Vertex cover number of a graph G* SimpleGraph.vertexCoverNum G\n* ν G* Matching number of a graph G* SimpleGraph.matchingNum G\n* ω G* Clique number of a graph G* SimpleGraph.cliqueNum G\n* ⍺ G* Independence number of a graph G* SimpleGraph.indepNum G\n* βₖ* k-subsets of β (Chapter 6)* {s : Finset β // #s = k}\n* N(s)* Open neighbourhood of s (Chapter 6)* openNeighborhoodFinset G s\n* χ G* Chromatic number of a graph G* SimpleGraph.chromaticNumber G\n* G⟦v⟧* Connected component of G containing v* connectedComponentMk G v\n* λ(G)* Edge connectivity of a graph G* SimpleGraph.edgeConnectivity G\n* κ(G)* Vertex connectivity of a graph G* SimpleGraph.vertexConnectivity G\n* e i* Basis vector of Fin n → Bool (open scoped hypercubeHamming)* Pi.single i true\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix","header":"15.1. Notation","id":"/Appendix/#section-notation"}});